.el .ds Aq '
.TH KWINFO-CLI 1 "" "KWinfo 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
kwinfo\-cli \- Command line companion to KWinfo
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkwinfo\-cli\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIcommand\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkwinfo\-cli\fR runs the sensor backends of \fBkwinfo\fR(1) without a window. It lists what they read, shows what the privileged helper adds, bundles diagnostic reports, and captures snapshots and recordings of the sensor files that \fBkwinfo \-\-replay\fR plays back on any computer: for comparing with \fBsensors\fR(1), for bug reports and for test fixtures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS list
\fBkwinfo\-cli list\fR [\fB\-\-mock\fR] [\fB\-\-replay\fR] [\fB\-\-fahrenheit\fR] [\fB\-\-ids\fR]
.PP
List every device and channel with its current value
.TP
\fB\-\-mock\fR
Use the synthetic mock backend instead of real hardware
.TP
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run the real backends against a captured tree instead of / (the output of \fBkwinfo\-cli snapshot\fR, or a test fixture)
.TP
\fB\-\-fahrenheit\fR
Show temperatures in Fahrenheit
.TP
\fB\-\-ids\fR
Show the stable id of every device and channel
.SS helper
\fBkwinfo\-cli helper\fR [\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-fahrenheit\fR]
.PP
Show what the privileged helper reads: through the system service, or with \-\-session from a helper started with pkexec for this command
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR
Start the helper with pkexec (asks for an administrator password) instead of using the system service
.TP
\fB\-\-fahrenheit\fR
Show temperatures in Fahrenheit
.SS report
\fBkwinfo\-cli report\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-mock\fR] [\fB\-\-replay\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-inventory\fR]
.PP
Bundle the newest diagnostic logs, a machine summary, the configuration and the sensor inventory into one text file to attach to a bug report
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
File to write (default: a timestamped file next to the logs)
.TP
\fB\-\-mock\fR
Take the inventory from the mock backend
.TP
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Take the inventory from a captured tree
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-inventory\fR
Leave the sensor inventory out (no hardware access, faster)
.SS snapshot
\fBkwinfo\-cli snapshot\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] <\fB\-\-out\fR>
.PP
Copy the sensor\-relevant parts of /sys and /proc into a directory, with serial numbers, WWNs and MAC addresses scrubbed, for test fixtures and bug reports
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to write; must not exist yet or be empty
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: /]
Capture from this tree instead of / (e.g. to re\-scrub an older capture)
.SS record
\fBkwinfo\-cli record\fR [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] <\fB\-\-out\fR>
.PP
Take a snapshot and then record every value that changes, frame by frame, so that \fB\-\-replay\fR shows usage, rates and temperatures moving as they did
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to write; must not exist yet or be empty
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 60s]
How long to record: 90, 90s, 2m or 500ms
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<MS>\fR [default: 1000]
Time between frames in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: /]
Record from this tree instead of /
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 after an error, which is described on standard error; 2 for a usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBKWINFO_BACKEND\fR
\fImock\fR makes \fBlist\fR use the synthetic sensors, as \fB\-\-mock\fR does.
.TP
\fBKWINFO_LOG\fR
What goes to standard error, in the filter syntax of the Rust tracing library (default: warn).
.TP
\fBKWINFO_FILE_LOG\fR
What goes to the log file (default: debug for KWinfo, info for the libraries).
.TP
\fBKWINFO_LOG_DIR\fR
Directory for the log files.
.TP
\fBKWINFO_NO_FILE_LOG\fR
Anything but 0 turns the log file off.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkwinfo\-cli list \-\-ids\fR
Every sensor with its value and the stable id that the settings file uses.
.TP
\fBkwinfo\-cli helper \-\-session\fR
Starts the helper through \fBpkexec\fR(1) for this command and shows what it reads.
.TP
\fBsudo kwinfo\-cli snapshot \-\-out\fR \fImy\-machine\fR
Captures the sensor files, including the RAPL counters only root may read, with serial numbers and MAC addresses scrubbed.
.TP
\fBkwinfo\-cli record \-\-duration 2m \-\-out\fR \fImy\-machine\fR
Two minutes of readings for \fBkwinfo \-\-replay\fR \fImy\-machine\fR.
.TP
\fBkwinfo\-cli report\fR
One text file to attach to a bug report.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at \fIhttps://github.com/kywa92/KWinfo/issues\fR and attach the file that \fBkwinfo\-cli report\fR writes.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBkwinfo\fR(1), \fBkwinfo\-helper\fR(8), \fBsensors\fR(1), \fBsmartctl\fR(8)
